// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Max Altgelt (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-04-06 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1127, T1059.007
// Description: Detects the execution of other scripts using the Node executable packaged with Adobe Creative
//   Cloud
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/mttaggart/status/1511804863293784064
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_node_adobe_creative_cloud_abuse.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\Adobe Creative Cloud Experience\\libs\\node.exe" and (not(ProcessCommandLine contains "Adobe Creative Cloud Experience\\js"))
